Note: Tuple literal + index + structural equality + empty + singleton (TUP-09)
Note: Tests: <<a, b, c>> literal, <<>> empty, <<x>> singleton, tup@N indexing, structural eq

use "@std"

Note: ===== Test 1: literal + index =====
Note: Plan named the example pair Note+Beat but Beat has no direct literal in 26.1
Note: (see plan 26.1-03 SUMMARY deviation). Use Note+Note instead — same code paths.
Tuple<<Note, Note>> entry = <<C4, D4>>
Note pitch = entry@0
Note other = entry@1
(print (str pitch))
(print (str other))

Note: ===== Test 2: empty + singleton =====
Tuple<<>> nothing = <<>>
Tuple<<Note>> just = <<C4>>
(print (str just@0))

Note: ===== Test 3: structural equality =====
Bool sameAB = (equals <<1, 2>> <<1, 2>>)
Bool diffAB = (equals <<1, 2>> <<1, 3>>)
(print (str sameAB))
(print (str diffAB))

Note: ===== Test 4: heterogeneous types =====
Tuple<<Int, String, Bool>> mixed = <<42, "hello", true>>
(print (str mixed@0))
(print (str mixed@1))
(print (str mixed@2))

